# SWGL has no span path for box shadows.
#
# ps_quad_box_shadow has only pattern_fragment(), so every box shadow pixel
# goes through the generic four-pixel fragment path. Per group of four pixels
# that costs a nine-patch texture sample, four corner half-space tests, an
# ellipse distance, a rect distance - and, because the shader rebuilds its
# constants from the flat varyings every time, eight divisions plus the plane
# and bounds setup.
#
# Almost none of that varies along a span:
#
#   - Every input to the distance field is a flat varying, so the plane
#     normals, plane constants, inverse radii and element bounds are the same
#     for every pixel of every span of the draw call. The shader cannot hoist
#     them into the vertex shader because that costs varyings, and this shader
#     already sits close to the GLES3 minimum of 15 (see the comment on
#     vElemCenter_Radius_TL and bug 2043249). A span path can memoize them
#     instead.
#
#   - A corner's half-space test selects that corner's ellipse only on one side
#     of the diagonal through the corner. Everywhere else the rounded-rect
#     distance is exactly signed_distance_rect(), whose gradient has unit
#     length. aa_range is the reciprocal of fwidth(local_pos), so the coverage
#     argument then moves by at most one per pixel, and a saturated coverage -
#     the element clipping the shadow out entirely, or not clipping it at all -
#     can be carried across a run of pixels from a single evaluation.
#
#   - The nine-patch clamp pins the UV to a constant across the middle region,
#     so a run that is both fully covered and inside that region is one solid
#     color.
#
# swgl_commitBoxShadowRGBA8() walks the span as a sequence of such runs: a
# solid color, a textured run with no distance field work at all, or - only in
# the anti-aliased band and on the corner side of a diagonal - a single chunk
# of the full per-pixel evaluation. On a 320x180 card with an 8px radius and a
# 12px blur, 74% of the pixels are a solid transparent run, 20% are textured
# runs and 5% still need the distance field.
#
# The run bounds were checked against a per-pixel evaluation over 71M pixels of
# randomized element rects, radii, nine-patch parameters and span steps: no
# pixel differs by more than the 1/255 output quantum.
#
# The decomposition is not ia64 specific - it applies to every SWGL platform.
#
# Rebased onto 158 (it had stopped applying): the hir.rs declaration lost its
# anchor, swgl_commitGradientRGBA8, and now follows swgl_commitColorR8; and
# vElemShape only exists under WR_FEATURE_SUPERELLIPSE, so the span's shape
# test is guarded. Measured on an Itanium 2 (Montecito) in the T2 SWGL
# benchmark, cycles per pixel, byte-identical to the fragment shader on an
# outset, an inset and a fractional-geometry shadow:
#
#                        fragment shader   span   x86-64 fragment
#   box shadow                366.3         55.3        98.7
#   box shadow inset          366.2         58.2        98.3
#   box shadow odd            366.8         56.5        98.1

